WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.870
This example shows an unnormalized appointment
record The row contains

00:00:05.884 --> 00:00:11.620
patient information provider information appointment
time a comma-separated list of service codes

00:00:11.791 --> 00:00:17.306
and a matching list of charges That design creates
several problems

00:00:19.031 --> 00:00:23.452
A foreign key cannot easily validate each service
code inside a comma-separated

00:00:23.478 --> 00:00:28.994
list Joining to one service is difficult The charges
can become

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:34.507
misaligned with the service codes The row also mixes
several different subjects

00:00:36.219 --> 00:00:40.377
Before normalizing state the problem clearly one row
is trying to represent

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:45.695
an appointment and several service occurrences at
the same time The first

00:00:45.722 --> 00:00:50.735
normalization step will separate those repeated
service values into individual rows
